Chapter: QuotesForged

  cites Foreword chapter Console
  quotes "sha256:71f85b21050759c45724ab3a7eebe9eb36453b16b5c3878c6fdea78732bce71b" as Sorted
  trusting "fcfbf1f0f3f0f3ff" "30a23f41fc17ec2aac012d0755750484a535afbcff80882094d569bbc7bdefff" 10000
  trusting above 5000

 The content is the real work and it hashes to the digest it was quoted
 by, so the first two guards are satisfied by an attacker who simply
 copied it. The signer named on the work is a key we hold and trust
 above the floor, so the third and fourth would be satisfied too, if the
 signature were real.

 It is not. One byte of it has been changed. Only verifying the
 signature against the signer's public key can tell the difference
 between a work alice signed and a work that merely says alice.

Section: Body

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
    print-line-uni ("sorted=" & show (sort-ascending 5))
  end

